                <div class="col-lg-7">
                    <h1 class="font-weight-light">Welcome to Apostolic Holy Convention 2026!</h1>
                    <h4>Theme: “There Must Be Something in the Water”</h4>
                    <h6><i>“But whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst…” — John 4:14</i></h6>
                    <p>Greetings in the Name of our Lord and Savior, Jesus Christ,</p>
                    <p>
To all the beloved of the Apostolic Dominion Holy Church of Jesus Christ—and to every visiting soul that has crossed the threshold of this Apostolic Holy Convention—I greet you in the most powerful, matchless, miracle-working Name: JESUS!</p>

<p>Welcome to the Apostolic Holy Convention 2026, where our theme is: “There Must Be Something in the Water!”</p>

<p>Just as Jesus met the Samaritan woman at the well, we have gathered around a divine wellspring. She came carrying questions, disappointments, and empty vessels, but she left transformed because she encountered the Living Water. That's why I declare to you today: There must be something in the water! Lives are changing. Chains are breaking. Hearts are being healed. Souls are being restored. There is something flowing in this atmosphere that only Jesus can provide.</p>

<p>This is not just another meeting, not just another moment—this is a divine move and a supernatural summons. The heavens are open, the fire is falling, and the saints are rising because “His Name Is Jesus!”

We have stepped into a God-appointed season, and as your Apostle, I must declare: “God arranged the change!” It wasn't a breakdown—it was a breakthrough. It wasn't rejection—it was redirection. Everything that shifted in your life, every closed door, every delayed answer, every unexpected turn—God orchestrated it to bring you here, right on time.

Like the Samaritan woman, some of us arrived carrying empty buckets and hidden burdens. Some came thirsty for answers, thirsty for peace, thirsty for purpose. But before this convention is over, you'll discover that what you've been searching for isn't in the bucket—it's in the well. And that well is Jesus Christ. That's why I keep saying: There must be something in the water!

We're not just attending a conference; we're walking through a door. And this weekend, we're coming with fire, hunger, and purpose!</p>

<p>Wednesday Night, we rise in strength with Pastor Rashon Gibbons for Men's Night.<br><hr>

Thursday Night, be empowered with Apostle Elizabeth Pierce for Women's Night.<br><hr>

Friday Night, receive your breakthrough with Apostle Emmanuel Cooper for Apostle's Night.<br><hr>

Saturday Morning, we invest in the future on Youth Day with Elder Edward Brownlee.<br><hr>

Saturday Night, we remember the foundation and fuel the vision at Founders Night with Apostle Charles Marsh.<br><hr>

And Sunday at 12 Noon, we close in divine order and Holy Ghost power on Official Day with Apostle Matthew Eady.<br><hr>

But let me tell you something right now:

“You got grace in every place.”

Wherever life has planted you, grace was already waiting. In the storm, in the fire, in the dark, in the dry place—grace was there. You didn't survive because you were strong; you survived because grace carried you.

And if grace carried you this far, imagine what Living Water can do for you now. The woman at the well came thirsty and left overflowing. She came broken and left believing. She came alone and left evangelizing an entire city. Why? Because there was something in the water!

Some of you are wondering why the process was painful, why you've been torn open and bruised. But hear me:

“The gift has to be ripped to get what's inside.”

The tear was necessary. The breaking was divine. God was unwrapping your calling. You thought it was destruction—but it was destiny being revealed.

“Another one bites the dust” may sound like defeat, but in this Kingdom it's a victory cry. Everything not like God—let it die. Every chain, every cycle, every addiction, every weight—bury it here at the altar. Some things had to fall so the real you could rise.

And now I speak as your Apostle with urgency and clarity:

Don't look back.

Don't stand still.

Don't freeze in fear.

Live forward!

The church has too many people dwelling in memories instead of moving in mission. The glory cloud is not behind us—it's ahead. The revival is not coming—it's here.

The woman at the well could have stayed trapped in yesterday's failures, but one encounter with Jesus changed her future forever. When you drink from what God is offering, you can't stay the same. When Living Water touches your life, your testimony starts flowing.

But be careful...

Don't follow the noise—follow the sound.

Noise is hype.

Sound is heaven.

Noise fades.

Sound carries.

Noise excites.

Sound births movements.

And the sound we hear now is the sound of Jesus. The same Jesus who sat beside a well and transformed a forgotten woman into a witness. The same Jesus who heals, saves, delivers, restores, and reigns.

So I charge you all:

Walk worthy.

Live holy.

Pray harder.

Praise louder.

Worship deeper.

Love each other without condition.

Let's kill the gossip, crucify the flesh, and provoke one another to good works.

Because guess what?

“God has prepared a table before you in the presence of your enemies.”

And I say to you:

Pull up a seat—and get ready to eat!

What God has blessed, no man can curse. What God has opened, no devil can shut. What God has ordained, you don't need man to validate.

As we gather around this spiritual well, I invite every thirsty soul to come and drink. Drink until your fears are washed away. Drink until your faith is renewed. Drink until your purpose is revealed. Drink until your praise overflows.

Because if lives are changing, if chains are breaking, if miracles are happening, if revival is spreading from heart to heart and city to city, then all I can say is:

THERE MUST BE SOMETHING IN THE WATER!

This is the hour.

This is the house.

This is the move.

One Lord.

One Faith.

One Baptism.

And ONE Name under Heaven whereby we must be saved—

JESUS!
</p>
<p>God bless you and welcome to the Apostolic Holy Convention 2026.</p>

<p>Apostle Matthew Eady <br>
Senior Pastor & Presiding Apostle<br>
Apostolic Dominion Holy Church of Jesus Christ</p>
