            <div class="row gx-4 gx-lg-5">
                <div class="col-md-4 mb-5">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h2 class="card-title">Pastor Rashon Gibbons</h2>
                            <img src="/images/gibbons.PNG" alt="" class="preacher-photo">
                            <p class="card-text" >Elder Rashan Gibbons, son of Rochelle Walker and Samuel Gibbons, was born August 3, 1989, in the city of Swainsboro, Georgia, where he yet resides. He is the husband of Brittany Gibbons. The Father of Lyndsey, Lyndon, Rashan Jr. and Riley James Gibbons. He was educated in Emanuel County Public School System. He also attended East GA State College. Elder Rashan Gibbons gave his life to the Lord at the age of 15 and was filled with the Gift of the Holy Ghost through the preached Word of God. He acknowledged his call to preach the gospel at the age of 20. Serving as Youth Minister and Muscian under the leadership of the Late Apostle Linda Stone Travett for 20 plus years. He served with great dedication to his leader and God. Elder Rashan Gibbons is deeply committed to the work of the Lord. He is a humble man of God that will assure you that if you only believe all things are possible through Christ Jesus. Due to the heavenly departure of his former leader Apostle Travett. He is now serving as Elder/Pastor of The Salvation Church located in the city of Swainsboro, GA, 30401, under the leadership of Bishop Anthony Chavers. Pastor Rashan Gibbons is a true Man of  God that has vision for church as well as community. One of his favorite statements is "COMMUNITY PLUS CHURCH EQUALS KINGDOM BUILDING!!!"</p>
                        </div>
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4 mb-5">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h3 class="card-title">Apostle Elizabeth Pierce</h3>
                            <img src="/images/pierce.PNG" alt="" class="preacher-photo">
                            <p class="card-text" >Apostle Elizabeth Brooks Pierce  is a dedicated servant of God, pastor, author, and community leader with decades of ministry experience. Called into ministry at an early age, she was saved and filled with the Holy Ghost at sixteen under the leadership of Bishop Patience Hopkins and faithfully served in various ministry roles before being ordained as an Evangelist in 1999.
In 2000, she founded  Mt. Moriah Tabernacle Deliverance Center  in Statesboro, Georgia, and later expanded the ministry to Thomson, Georgia. She was elevated to the office of Overseer and affirmed into the Apostolic Office in 2011.
Apostle Pierce is the founder and CEO of  LIC² Women’s Ministry  and  Two Fish Five Loaves , organizations focused on empowering women and serving those in need through mentorship, outreach, and practical support. She holds degrees in Theology, Christian Counseling, and Christian Leadership & Business.
Known for her prophetic gifting, dynamic preaching, and compassionate leadership, Apostle Pierce continues to impact lives through ministry, mentorship, and community service.</p>
                        </div>
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4 mb-5">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h3 class="card-title">Apostle Emmanuel Cooper</h3>
                            <img src="/images/cooper.PNG" alt="" class="preacher-photo">
                            <p class="card-text" >We are honored to welcome Apostle Emmanuel Cooper, Spiritual Leader and Founder of Emmanuel Temple Deliverance Churches. Apostle Cooper is a dynamic preacher, teacher, and servant of God who has dedicated his life to proclaiming the Gospel of Jesus Christ and equipping believers to walk in faith, holiness, and spiritual authority. Through his leadership and ministry, countless lives have been encouraged, strengthened, and drawn closer to God.

Known for his passion for deliverance, biblical truth, and Holy Ghost empowerment, Apostle Cooper carries a message that challenges believers to grow deeper in their relationship with Christ while inspiring them to fulfill their God-given purpose. We are expecting a powerful move of God as he ministers during Apostle's Night under the convention theme, "There Must Be Something in the Water."

Come prepared for a life-changing encounter as Apostle Emmanuel Cooper delivers a word that will refresh, restore, and revive thirsty souls through the power of Jesus Christ.</p>
                        </div>
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4 mb-5">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h2 class="card-title">Elder Edward Brownlee</h2>
                            <img src="/images/brownlee.PNG" alt="" class="preacher-photo">
                            <p class="card-text" >Elder Edward K Brownlee III is a native of Pembroke, Georgia.  He accepted Christ as his Lord and Savior at the early age of 13. Edward preached his first Sermon at the House of God Pembroke entitled “What kind of report do you have?”
Affectionately called “Brownlee” by many family members and friends, He meets no stranger and loves people! His heart for Ministry is exemplified every time he evangelizes both near and far!
He was licensed to operate for the Gospel Ministry as a Minister in 2009.
In 2017, he was ordained as an Elder and in 2018 he was appointed as the National Youth Overseer of the Gulf Coast Fellowship of Churches.
Elder Brownlee currently holds a Masters degree in Theology from Kingdom Ambassadors Global University.
He received spiritual training as he served under his childhood leader Pastor Jeff Spells! He served also under Overseer Elizabeth Pierce, Pastor Elizabeth Howard & Apostle Allen Jackson!
Currently he is found serving on the Board of Elders at Power of Praise Church of Deliverance in Opelika, Alabama, where Bishop Larry Torbert is his Overseer and Pastor!</p>
                        </div>
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4 mb-5">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h2 class="card-title">Apostle Charles Marsh</h2>
                            <img src="/images/marsh.PNG" alt="" class="preacher-photo">
                            <p class="card-text">We are blessed to introduce a true general in the army of the Lord — Apostle Charles Marsh, a man set apart for this end-time harvest. He serves as the Senior Pastor of Inner Circle Holiness Church in Rowland, North Carolina, where he leads with apostolic insight, prophetic precision, and unwavering dedication to the truth of God’s Word.

Apostle Marsh is a voice crying out for holiness and spiritual alignment, calling the body of Christ back to consecration and covenant. His ministry is marked by miracles, deliverance, and deep biblical revelation, as he equips saints to walk in power, purpose, and purity. With a shepherd’s heart and an apostolic mandate, he nurtures, builds, and governs according to the divine order of the Kingdom.

Those who sit under his leadership are not only taught but transformed. Through the ministry of Apostle Marsh, lives are restored, mantles are activated, and generations are empowered to stand boldly in the faith.

We honor Apostle Charles Marsh — a chosen vessel, an apostolic pioneer, and a faithful servant of Jesus Christ.</p>
                        </div>
                        
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4 mb-5">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h2 class="card-title">Apostle Charles Marsh</h2>
                            <img src="/images/eady.PNG" alt="" class="preacher-photo">
                            <p class="card-text">Chief Apostle Matthew Eady is the Founder and Presiding Prelate of Apostolic Dominion Holy Churches of Jesus Christ. Born in Hazlehurst, Georgia, he began preaching at the age of three and accepted Christ as his Savior at the age of five. From an early age, his ministry gifts were recognized, and he faithfully served in numerous leadership roles before answering the call to the apostolic ministry.

Throughout his life and ministry, Apostle Eady has remained steadfast through many personal tests and trials, continually witnessing the faithfulness and preserving power of God. Known for his passionate preaching, prophetic ministry, and unwavering commitment to the Gospel of Jesus Christ, he has dedicated his life to winning souls, strengthening believers, and advancing the Kingdom of God.

In 2018, the Lord directed him to establish Apostolic Dominion, a ministry devoted to preaching the Apostles' doctrine, promoting holiness, and empowering believers to fulfill their God-given purpose. Today, he provides spiritual leadership, mentorship, and apostolic oversight to churches, ministries, and leaders across multiple regions.

In addition to his ministry work, Apostle Eady is an accomplished information technology professional and software engineer. He holds a Master of Science in Information Technology and is expected to graduate in October with a Master of Science in Software Development. His commitment to both ministry and education reflects his passion for lifelong learning, excellence, and service.

A devoted father, Apostle Eady is the proud parent of Alyrra Alyse Eady, Aniyah Brielle Eady, and Zion Azai Eady. Affectionately known by many as “Pops,” he is respected for his wisdom, compassion, and dedication to helping others grow spiritually and walk in their divine calling.

His life and ministry continue to be marked by a steadfast commitment to the Name of Jesus, the preaching of truth, and the advancement of God's Kingdom.</p>
                        </div>
                        
                    </div>
